      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 131,
      "outputTokens": 948,
      "costUsd": 0.0085975,
      "pronunciationText": "So what does the shape mean? The curve is symmetric about its mean, mu. Fold it at mu and the two halves match. So half the area is on each side, which makes mu the median too. The curve is highest at mu, so mu is also the mode. Mean, median and mode are the same value. Most of the area sits close to the mean, and the curve gets lower and lower further out. That's why most bags land within a few grams of one seventy-five. Its tails get closer and closer to the axis, but never touch it. So the curve goes on forever, in both directions."
    },
