      "inputTokens": 117,
      "outputTokens": 797,
      "costUsd": 0.0072315,
      "pronunciationText": "We write X is normal, with mean mu and variance sigma squared, like this. The first number is the mean. The second is the variance, not the standard deviation. The bags are N of one seventy-five, sixteen, so sigma is the square root of sixteen, which is four grams. Change mu, and the whole bell slides along the axis. Make sigma bigger, and the bell spreads out and gets lower, because the total area has to stay one. Make it one and a half times as wide, and its peak drops to two thirds of the height."
