      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 865,
      "costUsd": 0.007849,
      "pronunciationText": "In a normal model, probability is still area. A bag is underweight if it holds less than one hundred and seventy grams. That's the area to the left of one seventy, and it runs all the way out to minus infinity. A single value has zero probability, so less than one seventy and at most one seventy give the same area. The model even gives a tiny area to impossible bags, like negative masses. For these bags, that area is so small it doesn't matter, so the model is still useful. A bag over one hundred and eighty grams is the area to the right, out to plus infinity."
    },
