      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 104,
      "outputTokens": 764,
      "costUsd": 0.006928,
      "pronunciationText": "One eighty is five grams above the mean, and one seventy is five below. So by symmetry, these two tails have the same area. And the bags between them are what's left over. That's one, minus both tails. The mean splits the curve too. Each half is exactly a half, so the bags from one seventy up to one seventy-five are a half, minus that left tail. You can find all three regions from one tail, using nothing but the shape of the curve."
    },
