      "pronunciationText": "The first number is the mean, so mu is sixty-four. The curve is symmetric with one peak, so the median and the mode are sixty-four too. The second number, thirty-six, is the variance. So sigma is the square root of thirty-six, which is six millimetres. A standard deviation of thirty-six is wrong. Thirty-six is sigma squared."
